{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And behold, afflicted with tzara'at.</b> There was no need to say this, since it had already been said ״וְהִנֵּה מִרְיָם מְצֹרַעַת״ etc. And according to the words of our Sages, may their memory be for blessing (Sifrei), who said that Aharon too was stricken with tzara'at, it intends to say: behold, she was still afflicted with tzara'at and it had not departed from her as it had from Aharon. Our Sages, may their memory be for blessing, further said there that specifically when he turned toward her she was afflicted with tzara'at, and when he turned his face away it would depart from her. According to their words, it is necessary to say that Moshe did not look at Miriam to know what she was, for if not, the difficulty stands either way (mimah nafshakh). Understand this."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:08:11.143699386Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}